From 109b137036c531149c1ed116162b9aed7900cb88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:55:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/78] h070: toglie la variabile special mai assegnata (SAS/C
 warning 94)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
---
 src_c/readable/backlog.md | 2 ++
 src_c/readable/h070.c     | 2 --
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src_c/readable/backlog.md b/src_c/readable/backlog.md
index d8ae1dc..6154ec8 100644
--- a/src_c/readable/backlog.md
+++ b/src_c/readable/backlog.md
@@ -2503,4 +2503,6 @@ Secondo passo di "Begin adventuring": i gestori dei comandi ECL di H064. Routine
 - **Controlli:** compilazione senza warning, controllo C89, build MinGW x86 e x64, ctest 8/8.
 - **Non provato:** Appraise con gemme vere, uscita con denaro nella cassa.
 
+**Correzione per SAS/C (warning 94 in h070.c, riga 754):** in `combat_end` la variabile `special` non era mai assegnata e serviva solo al `(void)`; tolte la dichiarazione e il `(void)`.
+
 ---
diff --git a/src_c/readable/h070.c b/src_c/readable/h070.c
index 008e1ce..e92c127 100644
--- a/src_c/readable/h070.c
+++ b/src_c/readable/h070.c
@@ -716,7 +716,6 @@ static void return_dropped_items(void)
 void combat_end(void)
 {
     Character *p;                       /* -$C(a5) */
-    u8 special;
 
     return_dropped_items();
     COK_PUT16(g_state_b + 0x58E, 0);
@@ -751,7 +750,6 @@ void combat_end(void)
                        "The monsters rejoice for the party has been destroyed.");
         show_message_wait(0x0D, 0, 0x19, "Press any key to continue");
     }
-    (void)special;
     H005_B(0x24CE) = 1;
     COK_PUT16(g_state_b + 0x6E0, 0);
     COK_PUT16(g_state_b + 0x6E2, 0);
-- 
2.43.0

